  "title": "Gloria M Possible NDE 6353",
  "date": "1963-65",
  "content": "It arose from a tonsil operation. In those days, they used a gas anesthetic applied through a facemask. Everything happened quickly, I lost consciousness. Then I felt and saw myself going through a tunnel at great speed, stopping at the end of it. There was a space or city, and a big lake preventing me going further. I was very scared, terrified, I could see no one. I wanted to go home to my parents and my house. I did not go back through the tunnel in reverse; I just woke up crying out for my parents and weeping. Subsequently, I was quite affected by the experience. I told my parents about it but they paid no attention. When I was small, just a few months old, I was in a coma, with sepsis, but I have no memory of anything like this. I have had other operations and have never had anything similar. Also it's true that I have never again had an anesthetic gas through a mask again, but different types of sedation or anesthesia.",
